(Ministry of Defense - Continuation of Off. No. 15669 GM/Aspar-MD, of 23/08/2018 - Fls 3/4)
its subitem B.2.4 - Content of the "classified information roll" area, reads classified document, with the aim of increasing transparency regarding its content, as well as allowing social control. It is emphasized that the inclusion of the subject in the list of classified documents assists in identifying future references, as provided for in Article 30, lit. e, of Law No. 12,527/2011. To this end, the agency must inform as broadly as possible the content of the document, without, however, revealing what the restricted information concerns. "This recommendation is simply ignored by the Army."

Response:
Article 30 of the AI (Access to Information Law) provides for the publication, annually, on an internet site, of rolls of classified and declassified information, as follows:

"Article 30. The highest authority of each agency or entity shall publish, annually on a website available for the dissemination of administrative data and information, in accordance with regulations:

I - a roll of declassified information in the previous 12 months;

// - a roll of classified documents in each level of secrecy, with identification for future reference;

f// - a statistical report containing the number of information requests received, fulfilled, and denied, as well as generic information about the requesters.

§ 1. Agencies and entities shall maintain a copy of the publication provided for in the preceding paragraph for public consultation at their headquarters.

§ 2. Agencies and entities shall maintain an extract with the list of classified information, accompanied by the date, level of secrecy, and grounds for classification."
